; pi-sandbox@0.6.2 declares peerOptional @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent@^0.80.0 while this repo
; pins 0.84.4, so a bare `npm ci` / `npm install` aborts with ERESOLVE. The pin is deliberate —
; 0.84.4 is the version the whole harness is verified against — and pi-sandbox works against it,
; its peer range is simply stale upstream. Without this file the lockfile can only be regenerated
; by remembering to type --legacy-peer-deps, which is exactly the kind of undocumented step that
; makes an install unreproducible. Drop this once pi-sandbox widens its peer range.
legacy-peer-deps=true
